"""Keep the references destination audit tied to the frozen GIS source table."""
import html,json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];d=json.loads((ROOT/'data/processed/campus-walk/destination-sources.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));esc=html.escape
rows=[]
for r in d['rows']:
 link='<a href="'+esc(r['official_gis_record_url'],quote=True)+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official GIS record</a>'
 if r['additional_official_source_url']:link+=' · <a href="'+esc(r['additional_official_source_url'],quote=True)+'" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University explanation</a>'
 rows.append('<tr><th>'+esc(r['model_name'])+'<small> Building '+esc(r['building_number'])+'</small></th><td>'+esc(r['gis_use_name'])+'</td><td>'+link+'</td></tr>')
block='''<!-- BEGIN DESTINATION GIS AUDIT -->
<section id="destination-gis-sources"><h2>Exactly which destinations were modeled?</h2><p><strong>This is a curated 22-destination model—not every campus teaching, dining or library location.</strong> The inputs are <strong>16 buildings tagged Classroom in GIS, 3 tagged Dining, Talley (tagged Student Center, added for dining using a separate university source), and 2 selected main libraries.</strong></p><p>“Teaching” and “Dining” are model categories. GIS <code>USE_NAME</code> is the original university building-use field. These data do not verify class schedules, hours, student access or actual visits. Buildings tagged Office or Laboratory may also contain classes, and small cafes and branch libraries are not exhaustively modeled.</p><p><a href="'''+esc(d['official_22_record_query_url'],quote=True)+'''" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the 22 records directly on NC State’s official GIS server</a> · <a href="'''+esc(d['official_layer_url'],quote=True)+'''" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GIS layer and field definitions</a></p><p><strong>Voting-site building tags:</strong> Talley is <code>Student Center</code>; Western Boulevard is <code>Office</code>. Those are the original GIS values, distinct from their use as polling sites. <a href="data/processed/campus-walk/comparison-site-gis-records.json">Original records for both comparison buildings</a>.</p><details open><summary>All selected destinations: model label versus original GIS label</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Destination</th><th>Original GIS USE_NAME</th><th>Original source</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</tbody></table></div></details><p>Talley’s GIS classification is <strong>Student Center</strong>, not Dining. Its dining role is supported by <a href="https://studentcenters.ncsu.edu/location/talley/">NC State Student Centers</a>. Hill and Hunt are the two selected main library destinations; Hill’s GIS wings are merged and counted once. <a href="https://www.lib.ncsu.edu/visit">The university lists additional library locations</a>.</p><p>The GIS active-building flag is not proof a building is open: closed Poe Hall was excluded despite its Classroom tag. Cherry Building was excluded because it lacked a usable entrance connection. The four missing housing routes remain excluded as described above.</p><p>Frozen GIS snapshot: '''+esc(d['gis_snapshot_date'][:10])+'''. The live official query was checked against all 22 frozen USE_NAME values on November 1, 2026; all matched. Live records may change after that check. The frozen record extract comes from the original dataset whose SHA-256 is <code>'''+esc(d['source_snapshot_sha256'])+'''</code>.</p><p><a href="data/processed/campus-walk/destination-sources.csv">All classifications and inclusion reasons (.csv)</a> · <a href="data/processed/campus-walk/destination-gis-records.json">The 22 original GIS feature records (.json)</a> · <a href="data/processed/campus-walk/official-gis-snapshot.zip">Complete original GIS data and hash manifest (.zip)</a> · <a href="index.html?view=1#campus-passby">Review the prototype</a>.</p></section>
<!-- END DESTINATION GIS AUDIT -->'''
p=ROOT/'report-source/article-references.html';t=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');start='<!-- BEGIN DESTINATION GIS AUDIT -->';end='<!-- END DESTINATION GIS AUDIT -->'
if start in t:
 a=t.index(start);b=t.index(end,a)+len(end);t=t[:a]+block+t[b:]
else:
 a=t.index('\n <details id="download-package"');t=t[:a]+'\n'+block+t[a:]
p.write_text(t,encoding='utf-8');print('Built prominently scoped 22-destination reference audit with original official record links.')
